# Default clang-tidy checks for C and C++ in any project under $HOME (linked to ~/.clang-tidy).
# A project's own .clang-tidy replaces this file, so projects can choose stricter or looser sets;
# clangd and the clang-tidy command both read it.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  modernize-*,
  abseil-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  concurrency-*
